1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Stop that horse!

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,166
Somebody stop that horse.

3
00:00:04,466 --> 00:00:06,532
He is running toward the river.

4
00:00:06,832 --> 00:00:08,232
The bridge is broken.

5
00:00:08,532 --> 00:00:09,732
Jump!

6
00:00:10,032 --> 00:00:11,498
I can't jump that far.

7
00:00:11,798 --> 00:00:12,998
Then swim.

8
00:00:13,298 --> 00:00:14,964
I don't know how to swim.

9
00:00:15,264 --> 00:00:16,464
Give me your hand.

10
00:00:16,764 --> 00:00:17,964
Hold on tight.

11
00:00:18,264 --> 00:00:19,464
We made it.

12
00:00:19,764 --> 00:00:20,964
You saved my life.

13
00:00:21,264 --> 00:00:22,464
It was nothing.

14
00:00:22,764 --> 00:00:23,964
Where do you live?

15
00:00:24,264 --> 00:00:26,330
In the village behind the hill.

16
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:27,830
Is it far?

17
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:29,596
About an hour on foot.

18
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:31,096
Let's go then.

19
00:00:31,396 --> 00:00:32,596
My feet hurt.

20
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:34,762
We can rest under that tree.

21
00:00:35,062 --> 00:00:36,528
Do you have any water?

22
00:00:36,828 --> 00:00:38,028
Only a little.

23
00:00:38,328 --> 00:00:40,061
Drink it; I'm not thirsty.

24
00:00:40,361 --> 00:00:41,561
What's that noise?

25
00:00:41,861 --> 00:00:43,127
It's only the wind.

26
00:00:43,427 --> 00:00:44,627
I heard a voice.

27
00:00:44,927 --> 00:00:46,793
Nobody lives in this forest.

28
00:00:47,093 --> 00:00:48,293
Someone does.

29
00:00:48,593 --> 00:00:49,793
Look, a light!

30
00:00:50,093 --> 00:00:51,359
It's a small house.

31
00:00:51,659 --> 00:00:52,859
Knock on the door.

32
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:54,359
Who's there?

33
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:57,192
Two travelers who have lost their way.

34
00:00:57,492 --> 00:00:59,358
Come in and sit by the fire.

35
00:00:59,658 --> 00:01:01,324
You are very kind, madam.

36
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:02,824
Are you hungry?

37
00:01:03,124 --> 00:01:04,324
Very.

38
00:01:04,624 --> 00:01:06,290
Here is bread and cheese.

39
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:08,190
Eat as much as you like.

40
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:10,956
Where are you going so late at night?

41
00:01:11,256 --> 00:01:13,389
To the city, to find my brother.

42
00:01:13,689 --> 00:01:15,889
The city is three days from here.

43
00:01:16,189 --> 00:01:17,855
Then we must leave early.

44
00:01:18,155 --> 00:01:20,355
Sleep now; I'll wake you at dawn.

45
00:01:20,655 --> 00:01:21,855
The sun is rising.

46
00:01:22,155 --> 00:01:23,621
The birds are singing.

47
00:01:23,921 --> 00:01:25,187
Did you sleep well?

48
00:01:25,487 --> 00:01:26,687
Like a stone.

49
00:01:26,987 --> 00:01:28,653
Thank you for everything.

50
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:30,819
Come back whenever you want.

51
00:01:31,119 --> 00:01:33,052
Which road leads to the city?

52
00:01:33,352 --> 00:01:34,685
The one on the left.

53
00:01:34,985 --> 00:01:36,651
Don't take the right one.

54
00:01:36,951 --> 00:01:38,151
Why not?

55
00:01:38,451 --> 00:01:40,584
There are wolves in those woods.

56
00:01:40,884 --> 00:01:42,684
We're not afraid of wolves.

57
00:01:42,984 --> 00:01:44,184
You should be.

58
00:01:44,484 --> 00:01:46,084
How much does this cost?

59
00:01:46,384 --> 00:01:47,584
Ten coins.

60
00:01:47,884 --> 00:01:49,084
That's too much.

61
00:01:49,384 --> 00:01:50,584
Eight, then.

62
00:01:50,884 --> 00:01:52,084
Agreed.

63
00:01:52,384 --> 00:01:53,650
Can I see the king?

64
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,350
Nobody sees the king.

65
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:57,516
Tell him his cousin is here.

66
00:01:57,816 --> 00:01:59,016
Wait here.

67
00:01:59,316 --> 00:02:01,049
The king will see you now.

68
00:02:01,349 --> 00:02:04,415
Your Majesty, I bring a letter from my father.

69
00:02:04,715 --> 00:02:05,915
Read it to me.

70
00:02:06,215 --> 00:02:07,415
I can't read.

71
00:02:07,715 --> 00:02:08,981
Then give it to me.

72
00:02:09,281 --> 00:02:10,881
This changes everything.

73
00:02:11,181 --> 00:02:12,381
What does it say?

74
00:02:12,681 --> 00:02:14,614
It says that the war is over.
